LGPL components (items 10 and 11): your rights
    These libraries are statically linked into the firmware images. Under the
    LGPL you may modify them and relink the firmware with your modified
    versions. Everything you need for that is public: the complete Faro source
    (Apache-2.0), the pinned MeshCore submodule commit, and the exact library
    and platform versions in envs/faro.ini and the MeshCore platformio.ini.
    Rebuild with `pio run -d external/MeshCore -e <env>` after replacing the
    library. The source of the LGPL components used by each release is
    available from the upstream URLs above at the versions listed in
    docs/THIRD_PARTY.md. For at least three years after each release we will
    also provide that source on request: open an issue at
    https://github.com/radek-sixi/sixi-tdeck-plus/issues.

